homelab-api (0.1.27) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship backup-paths.txt (/etc/homelab/api) so
    homelab-borg-service-backup-client's homelab_only mode auto-discovers
    this package's config without any hardcoded per-package knowledge.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 23 Aug 2026 18:00:00 -0500

homelab-api (0.1.26) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add Mail API Phase 4: send, save-draft, and allowed-from-address
    discovery. Sends via SMTP AUTH OAUTHBEARER against
    mail.mailmasker.org:465 using the caller's own JWT (no separate mail
    password), then best-effort files a Sent-folder copy that never fails
    the overall call. Supports reply threading (In-Reply-To/References),
    multiple attachments (local upload or by reference to an existing
    Drive file id), and enforces From-address authorization (against
    dovecot.allowed_sender_addresses) before any SMTP connection is
    opened. New endpoints: POST /api/v1/mail/send, POST
    /api/v1/mail/drafts, GET /api/v1/mail/allowed-senders.
  * Add Homelab::Drive::resolve_attachment_id for distinguishing file vs.
    directory vs. not-found when resolving a Drive attachment reference.
  * Config: mail.smtp.host/port now REQUIRED (fails fast at startup if
    missing), same as mail.imap.host/port. New mail.max_message_size_mb
    (default 25) caps outbound message size.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:13:35 -0500

